The build image now uses Gradle 8.13 / JDK 17 with Android Gradle Plugin 8.13.2 and Kotlin 2.2.20. During image build it compiles and unit-tests the included disposable Android fixture, then warms the Gradle dependency cache from that exact project. The job runtime remains offline and resource-limited. The image build itself is the authoritative proof that the Android SDK, plugin graph, and fixture work together.

From a trusted checkout:

```bash
export VIBES_WORKSPACE_SANDBOX_RUNTIME=docker
